    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Health",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6542\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to a review of reimbursement rates for ambulette trans-\nportation\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation would require the Department of Health to undertake a\nrate study for the Medicaid reimbursement of ambulletes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 requires an ambulette transportation rate adequacy review.\nSpecifically, the DOH will review the rates of reimbursements made\nthrough the Medicaid program for ambulette transportation as it relates\nto rate adequacy. These findings are to be reported to the Senate and\nAssembly.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPresent Medicaid reimbursement rates are barely adequate to cover the\noperating costs of these providers. Because of these low rates, ambu-\nlette providers across New York are ceasing operation. In order to\nbetter understand how to meet the financial needs of this industry, this\nrate study should be commissioned to look at Medicaid reimbursement\nrates. With a fresh review of rate adequacy, change can be implemented\nthat will help protect this vital industry by providing appropriate\nMedicaid reimbursement. Those being served deserve safe, professional\ndoor to door transportation to attend medical appointments so they can\nreceive needed critical treatments such as dialysis or physical therapy,\nas examples.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
